      "writtenOn": "2022-08-08T18:47:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it possible that this gets invoked twice? Since we invoke it even for the CLASSIC transport + with the classic address.",
      "revId": "d6ef9e35548a28fa87ca9d28cdc551dc2fbbe285",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "034be97f_1d165787",
        "filename": "system/bta/dm/bta_dm_act.cc",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 601,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132614
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-08T20:39:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Usually the classic address and the rpa are different.  Given MAC addresses have \u003c1% collision rate, I\u0027m not seeing them be the same.  Thus each call being in most cases unique.",
      "parentUuid": "28ee66c1_5c3143e4",
      "revId": "d6ef9e35548a28fa87ca9d28cdc551dc2fbbe285",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7eced527_3715effa",
        "filename": "system/bta/dm/bta_dm_act.cc",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 601,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958203
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-08T20:44:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess then, what is the purpose of cancelling a GATT connection to the classic address? And _only_ doing so if a _classic_ connection exists?\n\nIt seems strange to me that we invoke this GATT function differently depending on the presence of a classic connection. Either we should invoke it exactly once, on the RPA, or we should always invoke it twice: on the RPA, and on the identity address.\n\nBut right now this CL invokes it differently depending on whether or not we are connected using a classic connection, which I don\u0027t understand.",
      "parentUuid": "034be97f_1d165787",
      "revId": "d6ef9e35548a28fa87ca9d28cdc551dc2fbbe285",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b5e7006_f6dee3b8",
        "filename": "system/bta/dm/bta_dm_act.cc",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 601,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132614
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-15T17:31:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree it is a bit heavy handed.  Too bad bta_dm_remove_device doesn\u0027t accept address type.  So we don\u0027t know what kind of address this is.  If it is a classic one and we are removing the bond.  \n\nBoth transports get funneled here.\n\nWe don\u0027t know until we do the check to see if its classic connected in the bta_dm_remove_device.  If it is, we need to disconnect the ACL regardless of transport.  So yeah a conditional check would be ok to wrap around the gatt cancel connect. nbd.\n\nwe should invoke the disconnect peer always on all addresses.  I\u0027ll add the conditional for gatt disconnect based on transport.",
      "parentUuid": "7eced527_3715effa",
      "revId": "d6ef9e35548a28fa87ca9d28cdc551dc2fbbe285",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
