        "id": 1132614
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-08T20:39:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you are connected to an address of all 0s in which case you likely have a larger problem of having connected to a device with all 0s?  Otherwise someone else could reset the address in code somewhere later in the future?\n\n00:00:00:00:00:00",
      "parentUuid": "0c4cef2f_10f5c686",
      "revId": "d6ef9e35548a28fa87ca9d28cdc551dc2fbbe285",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1150f6c1_3e2a8692",
        "filename": "system/bta/dm/bta_dm_act.cc",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 620,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958203
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-08T20:44:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then why don\u0027t we also have this check for `bta_dm_process_remove_device`? \n\nOr in fact, why not then gate this whole thing (disconnection/device removal) inside an isEmpty() check? So if the classic address is empty, we skip anything to do with it.",
      "parentUuid": "9073bfd7_a507d664",
      "revId": "d6ef9e35548a28fa87ca9d28cdc551dc2fbbe285",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
